#   C:\temp\gmlc_v2\e911_lte_master_gmlc.csv
#
# for geographically abnormal PSAP allocation/routing.
#
#
# ROUTED PSAP RESOLUTION
# ----------------------
#
# PRIMARY:
#   GMLC.NENA_ID
#       -> Boundary.NENA_ID
#
# CROSS-CHECK / FALLBACK:
#   GMLC.PSAP_ID
#       -> Boundary.PSAP_ID
#
#   GMLC.FCC_PSAP_ID
#       -> Boundary.FCC_PSAP_ID / FCC_ID
#
#
# IMPORTANT
# ---------
# PSAP NAME IS NOT USED TO CHOOSE THE POLYGON.
#
# After IDs resolve the polygon:
#
#   boundary PSAP_NAME
#   boundary PSAP_NAME_ESRK
#
# are attached to the output.
#
# GMLC names are compared against the resolved boundary name only
# as data-quality evidence.
#
#
# EXPECTED PSAP
# -------------
#
# Caller coordinate
#       -> GeoPandas sjoin()
#       -> expected NENA_ID
#       -> expected PSAP_ID
#       -> expected FCC_PSAP_ID
#       -> expected PSAP_NAME
#
# Cell coordinate
#       -> same process
#
#
# CELL LOCATION
# -------------
#
# GMLC.SETUP_ECGI_DEC
#       -> CSSNG_DATA_ADDITION.ECGI
#       -> STRC_TOWERLATITUDE
#       -> STRC_TOWERLONGITUDE / STRC_TOWERLONGTITUDE
#
# Also retained:
#       ENB_ID
#       CELL_NUMBER
#       ONAIR_DATE
#
# If CSSNG coordinate is missing:
#       fallback to GMLC CELL_LATITUDE / CELL_LONGITUDE
#
#
# DISTANCES
# ---------
# All output distances are METERS.
#
#   CALLER -> ROUTED boundary
#   CELL   -> ROUTED boundary
#   CALLER -> EXPECTED boundary
#   CELL   -> EXPECTED boundary
#   CALLER <-> CELL
#
#
# FILTERING
# ---------
# Filtering occurs BEFORE expected-PSAP spatial joins for speed.
#
# Example:
#
#   MIN_CALLER_OUTSIDE_ROUTED_M = 19000
#   MIN_CELL_OUTSIDE_ROUTED_M   = None
#
# means:
#
#   keep calls where caller is >= 19 km OUTSIDE routed PSAP.
#
# Both None:
#   no distance filter; process/output all calls.
#
#
# OUTPUT
# ------
# psap_full_gmlc_abnormal_routing_candidates_v1.csv
#
# Plus QA summaries.
#
# =====================================================================


